plain java
---------
import java.util.*;

public class FindDuplicates {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[] arr = {1, 2, 3, 4, 2, 5, 3, 6};

        Set<Integer> seen = new HashSet<>();
        Set<Integer> duplicates = new LinkedHashSet<>();

        for (int num : arr) {

            if (!seen.add(num)) {
                duplicates.add(num);
            }
        }

        System.out.println(duplicates);
    }
}


java 8
------
import java.util.*;
import java.util.stream.*;

public class FindDuplicates {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[] arr = {1, 2, 3, 4, 2, 5, 3, 6};

        Set<Integer> seen = new HashSet<>();

        Set<Integer> duplicates = Arrays.stream(arr)
                .filter(num -> !seen.add(num))
                .boxed()
                .collect(Collectors.toCollection(LinkedHashSet::new));

        System.out.println(duplicates);
    }
}



E. Time and space complexity
Solution	Time	Extra space
HashSet approach	O(n) average	O(n)
Java 8 Stream approach	O(n) average	O(n)

Here, n is the number of array elements.
F. Choice of solution
Recommended: HashSet approach.




